<h2>Segment 250 &mdash; an animal makes its home</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s250S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w1">de nyid</span> la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w2">dud &#x27;gro</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w3">la sogs</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s250p1">pas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w4">gnas</span> kyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w5">blos</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w6">gnas</span> par <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w7">byed pa</span> dang</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s250S">An <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w2">animal</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w3">or such</span>, on the other hand, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w5">thinks</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w1">this same</span> water as a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w4">place to stay</span>, and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w7">makes</span> his <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s250w6">home</span> there.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s250p1"><span class="nul">Agent marking has no separate English word; subject relation is expressed by English syntax.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment reconciled by Codex (gpt-6-astra). The two gnas occurrences are distinct: the first names the perceived place to stay; the second carries the residence content home in GMR's makes his home idiom. Byed pa supplies its light verb makes, while par links the Tibetan predicate and is omitted. This local compositional match does not claim that every gnas par byed pa means making a home. The complete HGM glossary idiom and the separate gnas/home and byed pa/makes attestations support the split; his is supplied and stays unwrapped. De nyid owns this same; water supplies the antecedent from C05:249. Blos stays intact and owns thinks in the nominal-to-verbal recast, despite its separate glossary's intent reading. La sogs is the attested closing gesture or such and licenses initial or. Pas is retained whole as agentive marking with no separately alignable English word; it is not split into pa and s. The initial la and kyi are omitted as distributed relations. Final dang links onward in the source series; it is not assigned the English interior and. An, on the other hand, of, water, as a, and, his and there remain unwrapped. All original wording is preserved; no new erratum and no hgm_gloss promotion.</div>
<h2>Segment 251 &mdash; human perceptions and uses</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s251S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w1">mi</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p1">rnams</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p2">kyis</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p3">ni</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w2">mngar ba</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p4">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w3">dvangs pa</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p5">dang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w4">bsil ba</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w5"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m1">chu</span><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m2">r</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w6">rtogs</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p6">shing</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w7">&#x27;thung</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p7">ngo</span> , , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w8">khrus byed</span> <span class="u grammar" data-d="6" data-l="s251p8">do</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w9"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m3">de</span><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m4">r</span></span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w10">&#x27;jug</span></span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s251S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w1">Humans</span> look at the same thing and <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w6">perceive</span> it <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w5"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m2">as</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m1">water</span></span>--<span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w2">sweet</span>, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w3">clear</span>, <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p5">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w4">cool</span>. They <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w7">drink</span> of it, they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w8">wash</span> themselves with it, and they <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w10">swim</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s251w9"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m4">in</span> <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s251m3">it</span></span>.<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p1"><span class="nul">Plurality is fused into Humans; no separate English plural word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p2"><span class="nul">Agent marking is expressed by English subject syntax, with no separate English word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p3"><span class="nul">Topic marking has no separate English exponent here.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p4"><span class="nul">First list conjunction is rendered by comma punctuation, with no separate English word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p6"><span class="nul">Transition to the drinking statement is expressed by sentence division, with no separate English connective word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p7"><span class="nul">Assertive sentence closure, with no separate English word.</span></span><span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s251p8"><span class="nul">Assertive sentence closure, with no separate English word.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment reconciled by Codex (gpt-6-astra). Mi is human here; rnams contributes plurality fused into Humans, with no separate English plural word. Kyis and ni have no separately alignable agent/topic words in the English subject construction. The first dang is expressed by the comma after sweet and has no separate word; the second dang owns only the and between clear and cool. Chur is the whole inflected water word: its r licenses predicative as, so as water contains strict chu/water and r/as members. Der similarly owns the final in it after swim, with de/it and r/in members. Rtogs is captured once at perceive; look at the same thing and is a contextual expansion, not another atom. Shing's transition to drinking is expressed by the sentence boundary, with no separate connective word; ngo and do are wordless assertive closures. Khrus byed is the established washing construction and owns wash; no second make word is invented, and themselves with it stays unwrapped. The local water context and HGM 'jug/swim support swim. The genitive after bsil ba is omitted as the attributive relation recast across the postposed adjective list. Repeated participants, object expansions and the final English and remain unwrapped except the explicit der/in it. C05:252's initial go closes this row's 'jug across the preserved E-111 boundary-spill class. DVANGS/dvangs remains verbatim. No new erratum and no hgm_gloss promotion.</div>
